<Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before scaffolding.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use the `FLOW_VERSION` / `READINESS` fields from the `sdd-state` snapshot already produced by
        the skill's GATHER step; do not call `sdd-state` or `sdd-task` again here. Size the gate to this
        request's own blast radius (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`): v1 intersecting legacy task
        layout → `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/migration-v1-v2.directive.xml")`;
        not-ready and this scaffold needs a missing gate →
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/readiness.directive.xml")`;
        otherwise record the out-of-scope state in one line and continue.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED">
      The `FLOW_VERSION=v1` / `READINESS=not-ready` preflight gate protects scope-spanning work — a full
      migration or readiness setup dwarfs a narrow request. Size the gate to the task's own blast radius
      before firing it: when the requested change stays inside the entry point's own scope (a spec
      paragraph, a single ticket) and never touches the legacy v1 `tasks/` layout or a missing gate script, record the
      state in one line and proceed straight to the entry point's own work — offer migration / readiness
      setup to the operator as a separate next step, not inside this run. A change whose blast radius does
      reach the legacy v1 `tasks/` layout, task-ID rewriting, or a missing gate script fires the gate as before, ahead of
      the entry point's own work.
    </Axiom>